// The Salt Chapel after the first hunt (boss-sheets.md 6.3, saltmarrow-arc.md §4): the fight is the chapel's, the
// measuring was the fourth lighthouse's. At zero he withdraws; this is him saying so, by the altar, before he goes.
// He stands while the hunt is won and until he has spoken (FlagPresence), then the chapel is the salt's again.
// Halvard: Guild-formal, exact; paces and counts; enters silence as a plea. Not cruel: exact.

title: Chapel_Halvard_After
---
<<if has_flag("saltmarrow.chapel.halvard_spoke")>>
    Halvard: Entered. Go on, journeyman. The tide won't wait, and neither will the count. #still #face:wary #line:07e3a87
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Halvard: Three paces, and you closed them. That goes in the book as well. #face:wary #line:0d8bebc
Halvard: I am withdrawing. Not retreating. The Guild has a word for each, and I use the right one. #face:grave #line:0f8de5d
Halvard: Halden will hear the count. It will not hear that you were good. That part is mine. #face:grave #line:026d131
-> You could let me go. #line:06b0550
    <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
    Halvard: I am letting you go. Today. That is all the mercy a count allows. #face:grave #line:0a3808c
-> Next time I won't stop at three. #line:065234a
    <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
    Halvard: Next time I'll have measured four. Halden is a long way to grow. #face:wary #line:0428de7
-> Who told you I'd come this way? #line:0f16e6a
    <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
    Halvard: The reeds. Everything on this coast talks. Learn which of it lies, journeyman. #face:wary #line:05d5a56
<<flag saltmarrow.chapel.halvard_spoke 1>>
===
